From 9b87005d050668a5998fdc7a711cab40707aa6d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Chu <justinchuby@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:34:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support ONNX 1.23.0: new float6 types and opset 28

Backport of the source changes from
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/pull/32359 ("Integrate ONNX
1.23.0 base plumbing"), as merged in
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/commit/9b87005d050668a5998fdc7a711cab40707aa6d1

Upstream reverted that commit three days later in
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/pull/33073, not because of a
defect in these hunks but to wait for an ONNX release that fixes
onnx/onnx#8471 (external tensor re-save, fixed in ONNX 1.23.1) and
onnx/onnx#8529 (the C++ LastReleaseVersionMap still reports ai.onnx
opset 27, open).  The conda-forge build links the packaged libonnx
1.23.0 and cannot go back to ONNX 1.22, so it keeps the integration.

onnxruntime 1.30.0 was released against ONNX 1.22.  ONNX 1.23.0 adds two
TensorProto data types, FLOAT6E2M3 (27) and FLOAT6E3M2 (28), and bumps
the ai.onnx opset to 28.  Building 1.30.0 against the conda-forge
libonnx 1.23.0 therefore fails at compile time:

    onnxruntime/core/framework/tensorprotoutils.h:76:58: error:
      static assertion failed: TensorProto data type element-size map
      must cover every numeric data type.

because kTensorProtoDataTypeElementSizes is sized by
TensorProto_DataType_DataType_ARRAYSIZE and the two new slots default to
zero.  onnxruntime_map_type_info.h has an equivalent consteval
bijectivity check against the ORT element-type enum.

This backport takes every upstream hunk under include/ and onnxruntime/
that applies to 1.30.0:

  * add ONNX_TENSOR_ELEMENT_DATA_TYPE_FLOAT6E2M3/FLOAT6E3M2 to the C API
    enum and map them in both directions;
  * extend the element-size table with the two packed 6-bit types;
  * raise the maximum supported opset from 27 to 28 in the transpose
    optimizer and the CoreML/NNAPI/VSINPU/WebNN op builders, keeping
    Q/DQ builders at 27 where upstream did;
  * accept the opset-28 Cast in the attention, FastGelu, IsInf/ReduceSum,
    LayerNorm and Pad fusions, and the opset-28 Cast, Squeeze and Range
    in the EmbedLayerNorm fusion;
  * register opset-28 Mod (floating-point floor mod) on the CPU and CUDA
    EPs and opset-28 signed BitShift on the CPU EP, capping the previous
    registrations at 27 (and the DML BitShift kernel at 27);
  * honour session.allow_released_opsets_only on every model load path,
    and pass it through the Python onnx backend;
  * the matching C++ and Python test updates.

Upstream hunks deliberately omitted:

  * onnxruntime/core/providers/webgpu/compute_context.h -- an unrelated
    Logger refactor for the EP adapter API that does not apply to 1.30.0
    and touches a provider this feedstock does not build;
  * onnxruntime/test/optimizer/qdq_transformer_test.cc -- pins a test
    that does not exist in 1.30.0;
  * the cmake/, vcpkg, tools/, docs/, js/, csharp/ and requirements
    changes, which pin and test onnxruntime's own vendored ONNX; the
    conda-forge build links the packaged libonnx instead.

One hunk is adapted: the <type_traits> include in
onnxruntime/test/providers/cpu/math/element_wise_ops_test.cc is rebased
onto 1.30.0's include block.
